The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
if (cipher->ctx != NULL) {
    EVP_CIPHER_CTX_free(cipher->ctx);
}
```
Reason:
The bug occurs because the code assumes that the `ssh_cipher_struct` will always have a `ctx` field available, leading to a potential dereference of a NULL pointer when `HAVE_LIBCRYPTO` is not defined. If `cipher->ctx` is NULL, calling `EVP_CIPHER_CTX_free(cipher->ctx)` would result in undefined behavior.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
#ifdef HAVE_LIBCRYPTO
if (cipher->ctx != NULL) {
    EVP_CIPHER_CTX_free(cipher->ctx);
}
#endif
```
Reason:
The fix ensures that the call to `EVP_CIPHER_CTX_free(cipher->ctx)` is only made when `HAVE_LIBCRYPTO` is defined and `cipher->ctx` is non-NULL. This prevents the dereference of a NULL pointer and maintains the integrity of the code when the `ctx` field is not present in non-libcrypto builds.

